.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt MKIMG 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkimg
.Nd make a partitioned disk image
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar scheme
.Fl o Ar outfile
.Op Fl c Ar capacity
.Fl p Ar partition
.Op Fl p Ar partition ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes a disk image to
.Ar outfile ,
partitioned by
.Ar scheme ,
with one partition for each
.Fl p
in the order given.
Partitions start at 1 MiB and on 1 MiB boundaries, and are a whole number of
4 KiB blocks.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c Ar capacity
Make the disk at least this large, in bytes or with a
.Cm k ,
.Cm m
or
.Cm g
suffix.
The space after the last partition is left free.
.It Fl o Ar outfile
The image to write.
.It Fl p Ar type Ns Oo / Ns Ar label Oc Ns := Ns Ar file
A partition of
.Ar type
holding the image
.Ar file .
Blocks of zeroes are not written, so a sparse
.Ar file
gives a sparse disk.
.It Fl p Ar type Ns Oo / Ns Ar label Oc Ns :: Ns Ar size
An empty partition of
.Ar size .
.It Fl s Ar scheme
.Cm gpt
or
.Cm mbr .
An MBR disk has at most four partitions and 2 TiB.
.El
.Pp
The partition types are
.Cm oxfs
(GPT type
.Li 06026785-76ab-42c2-afe2-66ea3af562b8 ,
MBR type
.Li 0xa2 )
and
.Cm efi ,
an EFI system partition.
On a GPT disk the
.Ar label
is the partition's name, under which
.Xr devfs 5
lists it as
.Pa /dev/gpt/ Ns Ar label .
The disk's and the partitions' GUIDs are derived from the layout, so the same
partitions give the same image.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
A disk with one oxfs partition, the root file system:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mkimg -s gpt -o disk.img -p oxfs/rootfs:=root.img
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr makefs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_oxfs 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 10.1 .
This one is OxideBSD's own, with the same options for what it does.
